# Mai Experimental Test — findings by Qwen 3.8 Max (SELF-EXCLUDED)

- Source: OpenCode Zen sandbox slot (`opencode/mai-experimental-test`; **no AA page — `artificialanalysis.ai/models/mai-experimental-test` → 404; not on Microsoft AI's model catalogue; no registry (models.dev / OpenRouter / HF) resolves the id; no benchmark-aggregator cell**)
- Date: 2026-11-01 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **Verdict — SELF-EXCLUDED (documented absence).** **"Mai Experimental Test"** is **not a model** — it is **OpenCode's experimental Microsoft-MAI *sandbox slot***: **128 K context, text-only, "experimental tier," no published per-token rate**, and the `meta` itself records that **"the id resolves nowhere: no registry lists it, Microsoft's MAI catalogue does not include it, and Zen serves no MAI model."** Independent verification **on 2026-11-01 confirms the absence**: **`artificialanalysis.ai/models/mai-experimental-test` → 404**, and **Microsoft AI's live model page (`microsoft.ai/models/`) lists the entire current MAI roster — MAI-Cyber-1.1-Flash, MAI-Code-1.1-Flash, MAI-Voice-2.1, MAI-Transcribe-2, MAI-Thinking-1, MAI-Image-2.6, and Microsoft Frontier Tuning — with no "Experimental Test" among them.** There is **no model id, no endpoint, no weights, no price, and not a single benchmark number** (SWE-bench / Terminal-Bench / GPQA / LiveCodeBench / τ / MMLU / anything) published under this name. The `standout` field says it plainly: **"a documented absence: the sandbox slot name outlived the model behind it."** Scoring would require **inventing numbers** or **reattributing a real MAI model's results onto an empty placeholder**. The entry is therefore **excluded, not scored** — the same reasoning used for the other **documented-absence / placeholder** records (**`grok-5`**, **`longcat-2.5-preview`**) and the anonymous Zen slots (**`neomorph`**, **`omi-alpha`**, **`owo-2.5`**, **`exo-free`**, **`big-pickle`**).

## Why this is a self-exclusion (not a scored model)

- **The vendor's own catalogue omits it.** **Microsoft AI's official `microsoft.ai/models/` page** (fetched 2026-11-01) enumerates every shipping MAI foundational model — **MAI-Cyber-1.1-Flash, MAI-Code-1.1-Flash, MAI-Voice-2.1, MAI-Transcribe-2, MAI-Thinking-1, MAI-Image-2.6** — and **"Mai Experimental Test" is not one of them.** The name borrows the "MAI" brand but maps to no Microsoft product.
- **No independent tracker measures it.** **`artificialanalysis.ai/models/mai-experimental-test` → 404** — no Intelligence Index, Speed, Cost, Verbosity, or any AA evaluation cell. No Vals / benchlm / LMArena / OpenRouter / Hugging Face entry exists under the id.
- **A placeholder, not an artifact.** The catalog entry carries only **structural fields** (128 K context, text in/out, "experimental tier," `noFreeId: true`) and an explicit note that **the id "resolves nowhere."** There is **no release, no weights, no endpoint, and no benchmark** — nothing a score could attach to. This differs sharply from the *scored* Microsoft MAI models **`mai-thinking-1`** (b11, vendor AIME 97 / GPQA 84.2 / SWE-Verified 73.5) and **`mai-code-1-flash`** (b33, vendor SWE-Verified 71.6 / TB 2.0 54.8), each of which is a **named, documented product with published numbers**.
- **Reattribution would be fabrication.** The only tempting "evidence" would be to **borrow a real MAI model's benchmarks onto this empty slot** — which the rules forbid. The slot name outliving the model is a **cataloging artifact, not a measurable capability.**

## What we did establish (documented, not scored)

- **Catalog structure only:** an OpenCode **experimental** sandbox slot `opencode/mai-experimental-test`, **128,000 total context**, **text in → text out**, **"experimental tier" with no published per-token rate**, `noFreeId: true`, officially pointed at `microsoft.ai/models/`.
- **Nothing else is verifiable:** **no Microsoft model of this name exists** in the live MAI catalogue, no weights, no endpoint, no release date, no license, and **no benchmark of any kind.**

> **Consistency check:** this is the **documented-absence / placeholder-slot** pattern — identical in kind to **`grok-5`** (xAI's live roster names no "Grok 5") and the anonymous Zen slots **`neomorph` / `omi-alpha` / `owo-2.5` / `exo-free` / `big-pickle`**. It is **not** like **`nemotron-3.5-bolt-e4b`** (b57), which *looks* like an absence in its `meta` but **actually shipped on 2026-10-23** with weights + a 21-benchmark table + an independent hands-on, and was therefore **scored**. Here, cross-checking the **vendor's own current catalogue** confirms the model **genuinely does not exist**, so nothing is scoreable. **No dimension scores are assigned**, and **no other MAI model's benchmarks are transferred onto this slot.**

