- Future sources: this becomes scoreable **only if** Microsoft **publishes a real MAI model under this name with a model card + benchmarks**, or an **independent tracker** measures an artifact **under the `mai-experimental-test` id**. **Guards applied:** (1) do **NOT** reattribute **`mai-thinking-1`** (b11) or **`mai-code-1-flash`** / **`mai-code-1.1-flash`** scores onto this empty sandbox slot — the brand match is not a model match; (2) do **NOT** treat the `microsoft.ai/models/` landing page as evidence that this id "exists" — the specific model is absent from the enumerated catalogue; (3) the 128 K / text-only / "experimental tier" fields are **catalog placeholders, not measurement**; (4) **no numbers invented.** **No dimension scores are assigned.**
